@startuml seq-session-join
title Session join - mailbox command through relay handshake

participant "Game" as G
participant "libnetpak" as L
participant "DeviceCore\n(emulation thread)" as D
queue "SPSC out / in" as Q
participant "NetClient\n(net thread)" as N
participant "np64-relay" as R

== once, at NetClient start ==
N -> R : HELLO {proto ver, identity, room op}
R --> N : WELCOME {token, session, node_id}
note over N,R : token now carried on every frame;\nrelay re-pins source addr on any\nvalid-token frame (NAT healing)

== per join ==
G -> L : netpak_session_join("ABC123")
L -> D : CMD_DATA = "ABC123"; CMD = SESSION_JOIN
D -> D : CMD_STATUS = busy
D -> Q : control frame JOIN (seq=n)
Q -> N : dequeued (real time)
N -> R : JOIN (seq=n, token)
note right of N : reliable control plane:\nretransmit on RTO ~250 ms\n(doubling) until acked;\nJOIN handler idempotent
R --> N : JOINED {room, node_id, peers} (ack=n)
R -> R : fanout PEER_JOIN to room
N -> Q : JOINED into inbound SPSC
... next tick event (~0.5 ms emulated) ...
Q -> D : tick() ingests JOINED
D -> D : CMD_STATUS = ok; RES0 = node_id;\nIRQ_STATUS |= EVENT
D -> G : cart IRQ (IP3) if EVENT unmasked
L --> G : 0 (poll of CMD_STATUS or EVENT handler)
@enduml
